A||N||3||Diamond Joe Quimby||Noise from left rear wheel||||5||
Z||000000||Diamond Joe Quimby||08-03-2001||01:12 PM||||Just started driving my 84 after a long, long down time! Of course I already have something to fix, but at least the car keeps me from being bored on the weekends.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Here is the problem. When moving, I hear a noise from the driver's side rear wheel. It sounds kind of like the brake is dragging. I just did a complete brake job, so I thought it might just be everything settling into place, but it hasn't changed at all for 3 days. The weird part is that it gets substainially louder when making a right hand turn (making it the outside wheel), but not when turning left. Also, the wheel doesn't heat up, nor does the car pull at all when braking, so I don't think it is the brake dragging.<P>Haven't had a chance to really look into it, but I thought maybe someone would have some suggestions as to what it could be before I started messing with it.<P>any ideas?<P>thanks in advance,<BR>jim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fast85GT||08-03-2001||03:20 PM||||I would say that your most likely cause is, in fact, dragging - dirt.  Disc brakes are going to "warp" to an extent on corners - they flex.  Some times discs get crud under them and they make annoying noises for a long time.  They sell cleaners.  Other than that, check your U-joint, of course, and make sure that the Torx bolts holding the caliper is tight.  And just to be safe, check the lugnuts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeremy H<BR>Black 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-03-2001||03:36 PM||||Could be the metal backing plate behind the disc, rubbing the disk.<BR>Could also be a bad wheel bearing.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Diamond Joe Quimby||08-03-2001||03:47 PM||||Thanks guys. I'll make sure to check all the things you mentioned. I just hope it is something simple. I have put enough time into the car that I would enjoy at least one full week of driving it before I need to do any serious work on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-jim||||reg||1
